  "2026-09-17T04:42:52.786Z","harness:codex","Dependency correction based on live acceptance criteria and current implementation: full historical three-ledger reconciliation remains separate pm-q91qyd work. Exact candidate and previous registry acceptance reads published versions directly and does not depend on historical changelog backfill. Preserve the lineage as related rather than an unsatisfied ordering blocker; pm-rnl3sa remains a satisfied historical prerequisite."
  "2026-09-17T04:46:05.913Z","harness:codex","Live negative control: npm 12.0.2 npm pack --dry-run --json --ignore-scripts returns one keyed report; the artifact gate fails exactly-one-array validation before any size checks. Existing pm-xrjy8o and pm-7msh7k are closed shipped SDK/parser and runtime fixes; they remain closed. This residual release-gate consumer belongs to active released-artifact acceptance pm-ygli86 and is linked as verifying those contracts rather than duplicating or reopening their completed scope."
  "2026-09-17T04:47:23.616Z","harness:codex","Fresh remote telemetry correlation for the fixed ten-minute window 2026-09-17 04:30-04:40 UTC: 84 command starts matched exactly one finish by installation/session/command/start timestamp, zero missing finishes, zero duplicates. The bounded materialized-cohort query completed; an earlier unbounded join was canceled rather than left consuming database resources. This bounded observation does not assert completeness of every historical event."
  "2026-09-17T04:48:18.313Z","harness:codex",Consolidated overlapping historical linked-test commands into three non-overlapping executable groups while preserving immutable prior run history. Artifact controls and workflow contracts share one run; executor smoke and real packed CLI/MCP acceptance retain distinct runs.
  "2026-09-17T04:51:14.876Z","harness:codex","Manual branch-artifact acceptance: npm pack --ignore-scripts produced the current tarball; package gate passed 1531 files and 18472135 unpacked bytes under the unchanged 20000000-byte cap. Separate npm and Bun temporary installs resolved their own installed binaries; npx and bunx each passed seven lifecycle commands and complete public-SDK corpus reads. Packed-first-run additionally passed README initialization/create/list, MCP, real divergent Git merge/history verification, and detached telemetry delivery. npm 12 artifact receipt compatibility now accepts exactly one array or package-keyed report and rejects mismatched key/name identities."
  "2026-09-17T04:51:48.132Z","harness:codex","Removed the redundant reverse related row added during blocker correction: pm-q91qyd already records its association to pm-ygli86. The undirected lineage remains queryable without growing generic related-edge counts. Existing typed verifies and implements relationships carry the executable acceptance semantics. The unchanged related-edge ceiling caught this redundant metadata addition."
  "2026-09-17T04:55:59.231Z","harness:codex","Final acceptance verification: all three non-overlapping PM-linked test groups passed with zero failure categories; full repository suite and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage passed. Manual packed npm/Bun/npx/bunx and public SDK checks passed. Package-first dogfood passed when run after full coverage released the checkout lease; the earlier overlapping attempt correctly timed out waiting for that lease and is not counted as passing evidence. Hosted OS matrix execution and PR-head checks remain independent required hosted evidence."
  "2026-09-17T05:11:42.742Z","harness:codex","PR 1262 first-head CI: Windows unit acceptance fixtures did not supply the npm_execpath prerequisite and still recognized only the POSIX npm spawn shape. Correct the fixtures while retaining the production guard. Static failure is the separately corrected structured provenance gap. GitHub AI security review failed with HTTP 400 requested model unsupported; Sourcery reported its weekly review quota exhausted. These are unavailable reviews, not approvals."
  "2026-09-17T05:13:08.316Z","harness:codex","Windows fixture correction verified: all 13 installed-agent unit tests passed locally, including the explicit Windows npm entrypoint/refusal control; all three linked release test groups passed again. The native Windows hosted gate remains the cross-platform proof for the pushed revision. No production code or coverage thresholds changed in this follow-up."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T10:48:39.250Z","harness:claude-code","Measured 2026-07-26 against the published 2026.7.26: post-publish verification covers execution only. verify-published-release.mjs runs npx --yes <pkg> --version, npx --yes --package <pkg> -- pm --version, and bunx --bun <pkg> pm --version. No install path is exercised for any manager — not npm install -g, not a project install, not bun add, not pnpm add — so packaging omissions and binary-link defects reach users through a green pipeline. Confirmed working by hand and therefore available as a starting fixture: bun add @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.26 links pm, pm-cli, and pm-mcp, and pm init, pm create, and pm list all succeed under the Bun runtime. The third check's invocation shape is separately defective and is owned by pm-lpqln4."
